From 13247b3aca6853f1f994612dd33b9643ea50b910 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keith Packard <keithp@keithp.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 05:25:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/20] unistd.h: Give the V8 sysconf and confstr names their
 own values

The _SC_V8_*, _CS_POSIX_V8_* and _CS_V8_ENV names shared the values of
their V7 counterparts. POSIX allows only _SC_PAGESIZE and _SC_PAGE_SIZE
to be the same; an application switching on the names couldn't list
both. sysconf and confstr answer the V8 names as they do the V7 ones,
with V8 environment names in _CS_POSIX_V8_WIDTH_RESTRICTED_ENVS.
---
 libc/include/sys/unistd.h   | 40 ++++++++++++++++++-------------------
 libc/posix/unistd/confstr.c | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 libos/fallback/sysconf.c    | 24 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 31 deletions(-)

